IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pipa-dates`

-- Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) -- the pre-court procedure and the costs rules, as the CLAIMANT
-- meets them.
--
-- SEAT: the injured person (or the person claiming for a death or for a child) who wants damages for a personal injury
-- in Queensland, outside the motor vehicle and workers' compensation schemes. "Does this Act apply to me?", "By when
-- must I give my notice of claim?", "What if I am late?", "What must I give the respondent, and what must it give me?",
-- "When can I call the compulsory conference?", "When can I, and when should I, start my court proceeding?", "Can I sue
-- after the limitation period?", "Who pays the costs?". The respondent, its insurer and the court get no seat; their
-- duties appear as what the claimant is owed and by when.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list). The duties with deadlines
-- (part 1 of the notice, the initial notice, the parent's notice for a child, the claimant's documents, the bar while a
-- final offer is open, the 60 days to start) are DEONTIC rules run inside by EVALTRACE; no question takes a DEONTIC or
-- an EVENT. Judgments the Act hands to the court or the respondent (reasonable excuse, proper reason, unreasonable,
-- urgent need, leave, "as soon as practicable") are asked as facts, never decided.
--
-- Periods "prescribed under a regulation or, if no period is prescribed, ..." take the Act's own fallback period: the
-- Personal Injuries Proceedings Regulation is not deposited (NOTES.md, fork F3). The lower offer limit, the upper offer
-- limit and the declared costs limit are fixed by the Minister's notice under s 75A, also not deposited: they are asked.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002: the claimant's questions`

-- The parties and acts the regulative rules speak of.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `I`
    `my parent or legal guardian`
    `the respondent`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `give part 1 of my notice of claim`
    `give a reasonable excuse for the delay`
    `give my initial notice`
    `give the documents or information`
    `start my court proceeding`
    `apply to the court for an order that the claim not proceed`

-- The helper that runs a rule over one event. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not
-- BREACH or a residual rule. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
      `the party` IS A `Party`
      `the step` IS A `Step`
      `the time it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule is met` `the rule` `the party` `the step` `the time it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `the party` `the step` `the time it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 6 -- whether the Act applies to my injury`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 6(1) all personal injury arising out of an incident; s 6(2), (3) the exclusions ("does not apply to"); s 6(5) the
-- schemes the Act "does not affect". The exclusions are flat negatives: JUST FALSE kind, here "no" constructors. Which
-- scheme applies to an injury is a borrowed question (the other Acts are not encoded here): asked by choice.
DECLARE `What my injury is` IS ONE OF
    `a personal injury not covered by any of the other choices`
    `an injury from a motor vehicle to which the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 applies`
    `a work injury, and I seek damages from my employer under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 chapter 5`
    `an injury to which an earlier scheme named in s 6(2)(b) or (d) to (g) applies, to the extent stated there`
    `a dust-related condition`
    `a claim for financial assistance or damages under a scheme named in s 6(5), such as the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009`

DECLARE `Does the Act apply` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Act applies to my personal injury (s 6(1))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to a motor vehicle injury under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (s 6(2)(a))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to my damages claim against my employer; the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 chapter 5 regulates it (s 6(2)(c))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to the extent an earlier scheme in s 6(2)(b) or (d) to (g) applies`
    `no: the Act does not apply to a dust-related condition (s 6(3)(b))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to an injury for which a proceeding was started in a court before 18 June 2002 (s 6(3)(a))`
    `the Act does not affect a claim under the schemes in s 6(5); that scheme governs it`

GIVEN `the injury` IS A `What my injury is`
      `a proceeding was started before 18 June 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Does the Act apply`
`s 6 -- the Act applies` `the injury` `a proceeding was started before 18 June 2002` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the injury`
    WHEN `an injury from a motor vehicle to which the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 applies` THEN `no: the Act does not apply to a motor vehicle injury under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (s 6(2)(a))`
    WHEN `a work injury, and I seek damages from my employer under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 chapter 5` THEN `no: the Act does not apply to my damages claim against my employer; the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 chapter 5 regulates it (s 6(2)(c))`
    WHEN `an injury to which an earlier scheme named in s 6(2)(b) or (d) to (g) applies, to the extent stated there` THEN `no: the Act does not apply to the extent an earlier scheme in s 6(2)(b) or (d) to (g) applies`
    WHEN `a dust-related condition` THEN `no: the Act does not apply to a dust-related condition (s 6(3)(b))`
    WHEN `a claim for financial assistance or damages under a scheme named in s 6(5), such as the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009` THEN `the Act does not affect a claim under the schemes in s 6(5); that scheme governs it`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `a proceeding was started before 18 June 2002`
        THEN `no: the Act does not apply to an injury for which a proceeding was started in a court before 18 June 2002 (s 6(3)(a))`
        ELSE `yes: the Act applies to my personal injury (s 6(1))`

@export Does the Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) apply to my injury (s 6)? It applies to personal injury (including death, prenatal injury, psychological injury and disease) arising out of an incident, but not to motor vehicle injuries under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994, damages claims against an employer under the workers' compensation scheme, dust-related conditions, or an injury for which a court proceeding was started before 18 June 2002. It does not affect victims of crime assistance and the other schemes in s 6(5).
GIVEN `my injury` IS A `What my injury is` @desc What your injury or claim is: a personal injury not covered by any other choice (for example a fall in a shop, a medical injury, an assault); a motor vehicle injury under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994; a work injury where you seek damages from your employer under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 chapter 5 (a claim against someone else, such as a machine maker, is "not covered by any other choice"); an injury under an earlier scheme in s 6(2)(b) or (d) to (g); a dust-related condition; or a claim under a scheme in s 6(5), such as victims of crime assistance
      `started before 18 June 2002` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court proceeding (anywhere, including outside Queensland or Australia) was started for this injury before 18 June 2002
GIVETH A `Does the Act apply`
`Does the Act apply to my injury` MEANS
    `s 6 -- the Act applies` `my injury` `started before 18 June 2002`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 9 -- to whom I give my notices`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 9(1) part 1 goes "to the person against whom the proceeding is proposed to be started"; s 9(8) for the State or a
-- State entity it is effective "only if" given to the Crown solicitor, identifying the department or entity. s 9A(2)
-- the initial notice for a medical incident goes to the person; s 9A(7) for the State, "only if" to the health service
-- chief executive (a place controlled by a Hospital and Health Service) or the chief executive officer of the
-- department or entity in control of the place.
DECLARE `Who receives my notice` IS ONE OF
    `the person against whom I propose to start the proceeding (s 9(1), s 9A(2))`
    `the Crown solicitor, and part 1 must identify the government department or entity I consider responsible (s 9(8))`
    `the health service chief executive of the Hospital and Health Service that controls the place (s 9A(7)(a))`
    `the chief executive officer of the department or entity that controls the place of the medical incident (s 9A(7)(b))`

DECLARE `Which notice` IS ONE OF
    `part 1 of my notice of claim`
    `my initial notice for a medical incident`

GIVEN `the notice` IS A `Which notice`
      `the State is the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Hospital and Health Service controls the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who receives my notice`
`ss 9(1), 9(8), 9A(2), 9A(7) -- who receives my notice` `the notice` `the State is the respondent` `a Hospital and Health Service controls the place` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the State is the respondent`)
    THEN `the person against whom I propose to start the proceeding (s 9(1), s 9A(2))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the notice`
         WHEN `part 1 of my notice of claim` THEN `the Crown solicitor, and part 1 must identify the government department or entity I consider responsible (s 9(8))`
         OTHERWISE
             IF `a Hospital and Health Service controls the place`
             THEN `the health service chief executive of the Hospital and Health Service that controls the place (s 9A(7)(a))`
             ELSE `the chief executive officer of the department or entity that controls the place of the medical incident (s 9A(7)(b))`

@export To whom must I give my notice of claim (part 1), or my initial notice for a medical incident (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 9(1), 9(8), 9A(2), 9A(7))? Normally to the person you propose to sue. If that is the State or an entity with the State's privileges and immunities, part 1 counts only if given to the Crown solicitor, naming the department or entity you hold responsible, and an initial notice counts only if given to the chief executive of the Hospital and Health Service, or of the department or entity, that controls the place.
GIVEN `notice` IS A `Which notice` @desc Which notice: part 1 of my notice of claim; or my initial notice for a medical incident (the first notice in a medical negligence claim under s 9A)
      `against the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you propose to sue is the State of Queensland or an entity with the privileges and immunities of the State (for example a public hospital)
      `Hospital and Health Service place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an initial notice against the State: whether the place of the medical incident is controlled by a Hospital and Health Service; otherwise answer either way
GIVETH A `Who receives my notice`
`To whom must I give my notice` MEANS
    `ss 9(1), 9(8), 9A(2), 9A(7) -- who receives my notice` `notice` `against the State` `Hospital and Health Service place`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 9(3), 9A(4), 19 -- by when I give part 1 or the initial notice`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 9(3) part 1 "must be given within the period ending on the earlier of the following days-- (a) the day 9 months
-- after the day the incident giving rise to the personal injury happened or, if symptoms of the injury are not
-- immediately apparent, the first appearance of symptoms of the injury; (b) the day 1 month after the day the claimant
-- first instructs a law practice to act on the person's behalf in seeking damages for the personal injury and the
-- person against whom the proceeding is proposed to be started is identified." s 9A(4) is the same for the initial
-- notice, counted from the medical incident.
-- (b) is read as running from the later of the two days: the day both have happened (fork F4).
-- s 9(9A) and s 9A(13): a consultation with a community legal service is disregarded (it is not "instructing").
-- s 19: obligations under the division are suspended while I am under a legal disability (borrowed from the Limitation
-- of Actions Act 1974: asked); the period begins when it ends, and the day of the incident is read as the day it ends.
-- Read here as: neither limb's period starts before the disability ends (fork F5).
GIVEN `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
      `symptoms were immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE
      `I instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I first instructed it` IS A DATE
      `the day the respondent was identified` IS A DATE
      `I was under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the disability ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 9(3), 9A(4), 19 -- the last day` `the day of the incident` `symptoms were immediately apparent` `the day symptoms first appeared` `I instructed a law practice` `the day I first instructed it` `the day the respondent was identified` `I was under a legal disability` `the day the disability ended` MEANS
    IF `I instructed a law practice`
    THEN `the earlier of` `the nine months day` `and` `the one month day`
    ELSE `the nine months day`
    WHERE
        `the day counted from` MEANS
            IF `symptoms were immediately apparent` THEN `the day of the incident` ELSE `the day symptoms first appeared`
        `the start for (a)` MEANS
            IF `I was under a legal disability`
            THEN `the later of` `the day counted from` `and` `the day the disability ended`
            ELSE `the day counted from`
        `the nine months day` MEANS `the date` 9 `months after` `the start for (a)`
        `the instructed and identified day` MEANS `the later of` `the day I first instructed it` `and` `the day the respondent was identified`
        `the start for (b)` MEANS
            IF `I was under a legal disability`
            THEN `the later of` `the instructed and identified day` `and` `the day the disability ended`
            ELSE `the instructed and identified day`
        `the one month day` MEANS `the date` 1 `months after` `the start for (b)`

-- s 9(9C) "Subsections (3), (5) and (6) do not apply to a claim based on a personal injury of a person resulting from
-- the abuse of the person when the person was a child." s 9(9B), 9A(9)(c): for a medical incident under s 9A, s 9(3)
-- does not apply; part 1 is due "within 12 months after the respondent complies with subsection (8)" (9A(9)(b)), and
-- no day is fixed until the respondent complies.
DECLARE `Part 1 route` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary claim`
    `abuse as a child`
    `medical incident under s 9A`

GIVEN `the route` IS A `Part 1 route`
      `the respondent complied with s 9A(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it complied` IS A DATE
      `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
      `symptoms were immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE
      `I instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I first instructed it` IS A DATE
      `the day the respondent was identified` IS A DATE
      `I was under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the disability ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 9(3), 9(9C), 9A(9)(b) -- the last day for part 1` `the route` `the respondent complied with s 9A(8)` `the day it complied` `the day of the incident` `symptoms were immediately apparent` `the day symptoms first appeared` `I instructed a law practice` `the day I first instructed it` `the day the respondent was identified` `I was under a legal disability` `the day the disability ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `abuse as a child` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `medical incident under s 9A` THEN
        IF `the respondent complied with s 9A(8)`
        THEN JUST (`the date` 12 `months after` (`the later of` `the day it complied` `and` (`the disability day or` `the day it complied`)))
        ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (`ss 9(3), 9A(4), 19 -- the last day` `the day of the incident` `symptoms were immediately apparent` `the day symptoms first appeared` `I instructed a law practice` `the day I first instructed it` `the day the respondent was identified` `I was under a legal disability` `the day the disability ended`)
    WHERE
        `the disability day or` `the fallback` MEANS
            IF `I was under a legal disability` THEN `the day the disability ended` ELSE `the fallback`

@export By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 9(3), 9(9C), 9A(9)(b), 19)? The earlier of 9 months after the incident (or after symptoms first appeared, if they were not immediately apparent) and 1 month after you first instructed a law practice and the person to sue was identified. For a medical incident under s 9A: 12 months after the respondent answers your initial notice. No time limit for a claim for abuse suffered as a child. While you are under a legal disability (for example a child), the time does not run. No answer where no day is yet fixed.
GIVEN `route` IS A `Part 1 route` @desc Your kind of claim: ordinary claim; abuse as a child (sexual abuse or serious physical abuse when you were under 18, or psychological abuse connected with it); or medical incident under s 9A (an act, omission or circumstance involving a doctor while providing medical services, which needs an initial notice first)
      `respondent answered initial notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Medical incident only: whether the respondent has given you its written response and documents under s 9A(8) in reply to your initial notice; otherwise answer either way
      `day respondent answered` IS A DATE @desc Medical incident only: the day it did so, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day of incident` IS A DATE @desc The day the incident that caused your injury happened, as an ISO date such as 2026-03-14
      `symptoms immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the symptoms of your injury were immediately apparent when the incident happened
      `day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE @desc If they were not, the day the symptoms first appeared, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have instructed a law practice (a lawyer) to act for you in seeking damages for this injury; a consultation with a community legal service does not count
      `day first instructed` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you first instructed it, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day respondent identified` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the person you propose to sue was identified, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under a legal disability as the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 means it (for example under 18, or of unsound mind) when the incident happened
      `day disability ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it ended (for example your 18th birthday), as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` MEANS
    `ss 9(3), 9(9C), 9A(9)(b) -- the last day for part 1` `route` `respondent answered initial notice` `day respondent answered` `day of incident` `symptoms immediately apparent` `day symptoms first appeared` `instructed a law practice` `day first instructed` `day respondent identified` `legal disability` `day disability ended`

@export By when must I give my initial notice for a medical incident (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 9A(4), 19)? Before part 1 of a notice of claim for a medical incident, you must give the doctor or provider an initial notice. It is due by the earlier of 9 months after the medical incident (or after symptoms first appeared, if they were not immediately apparent) and 1 month after you first instructed a law practice and the person to sue was identified. While you are under a legal disability, the time does not run.
GIVEN `day of medical incident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the medical incident (the act, omission or circumstance involving a doctor while providing medical services), as an ISO date
      `symptoms immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the symptoms of your injury were immediately apparent
      `day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE @desc If they were not, the day the symptoms first appeared, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have instructed a law practice (a lawyer) to act for you in seeking damages for this injury; a consultation with a community legal service does not count
      `day first instructed` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you first instructed it, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day respondent identified` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the person you propose to sue was identified, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under a legal disability as the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 means it (for example under 18) when the incident happened
      `day disability ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it ended, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give my initial notice` MEANS
    `ss 9(3), 9A(4), 19 -- the last day` `day of medical incident` `symptoms immediately apparent` `day symptoms first appeared` `instructed a law practice` `day first instructed` `day respondent identified` `legal disability` `day disability ended`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 9(5), 9(6), 9A(6), 9A(6A) -- if I am late with part 1 or the initial notice`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 9(5) "If part 1 of the notice is not given within the period ... the obligation to give the notice under
-- subsection (1) continues and a reasonable excuse for the delay must be given in part 1 of the notice or by separate
-- notice". The rule: I DO give part 1 WITHIN the days to the last day; LEST I MUST give a reasonable excuse (and the
-- obligation to give part 1 continues). Days are counted from the day the period runs from (time 0).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 9(3), (5) -- give part 1 in time, or with an excuse` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `give part 1 of my notice of claim`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `I`
        MUST `give a reasonable excuse for the delay`

-- s 9A(6) the same for the initial notice: the excuse "must be given in the initial notice".
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 9A(4), (6) -- give the initial notice in time, or with an excuse` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `give my initial notice`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `I`
        MUST `give a reasonable excuse for the delay`

-- Given on or before the last day? Time 0 is the day the earliest limb runs from; a notice given before then is in
-- time.
GIVEN `the rule maker` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
      `the step` IS A `Step`
      `the day counted from` IS A DATE
      `the last day` IS A DATE
      `the day given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `given by the last day under` `the rule maker` `the step` `the day counted from` `the last day` `the day given` IF
    IF `the day` `the day given` `is before` `the day counted from`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `the rule is met` (`the rule maker` (`the days from` `the day counted from` `to` `the last day`)) `I` `the step` (`the days from` `the day counted from` `to` `the day given`)

-- s 9(6), 9A(6A): "the claimant is taken to have a reasonable excuse ... if" the claimant made a health service
-- complaint about the person (to the Health Rights Commissioner or the Health Quality and Complaints Commission within
-- the time for it, or to the health ombudsman within 2 years after becoming aware of the matter) and gives the notice
-- "as soon as practicable after the complaint is finalised". Both limbs are asked (the second is a judgment).
DECLARE `Was I late` IS ONE OF
    `in time: I give it by the last day`
    `late: the duty to give it continues, and I must give a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 9(5), s 9A(6))`
    `late, but I am taken to have a reasonable excuse because of my health service complaint (s 9(6), s 9A(6A))`
    `no time limit: s 9(3), (5) and (6) do not apply to a claim for abuse as a child (s 9(9C))`
    `no day fixed yet: part 1 for a medical incident is due 12 months after the respondent answers my initial notice (s 9A(9)(b))`

GIVEN `in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made a health service complaint in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Was I late`
`ss 9(5), 9(6) -- what follows` `in time` `I made a health service complaint in time` `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `in time`
        THEN `in time: I give it by the last day`
        IF `I made a health service complaint in time` AND `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised`
        THEN `late, but I am taken to have a reasonable excuse because of my health service complaint (s 9(6), s 9A(6A))`
        OTHERWISE `late: the duty to give it continues, and I must give a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 9(5), s 9A(6))`

GIVEN `the route` IS A `Part 1 route`
      `the respondent complied with s 9A(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it complied` IS A DATE
      `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
      `symptoms were immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE
      `I instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I first instructed it` IS A DATE
      `the day the respondent was identified` IS A DATE
      `I was under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the disability ended` IS A DATE
      `the day given` IS A DATE
      `I made a health service complaint in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Was I late`
`ss 9(5), 9(6) -- was I late with part 1` `the route` `the respondent complied with s 9A(8)` `the day it complied` `the day of the incident` `symptoms were immediately apparent` `the day symptoms first appeared` `I instructed a law practice` `the day I first instructed it` `the day the respondent was identified` `I was under a legal disability` `the day the disability ended` `the day given` `I made a health service complaint in time` `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day`
    WHEN JUST `the due day` THEN
        `ss 9(5), 9(6) -- what follows` (`given by the last day under` `s 9(3), (5) -- give part 1 in time, or with an excuse` `give part 1 of my notice of claim` `the earliest start` `the due day` `the day given`) `I made a health service complaint in time` `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the route` EQUALS `abuse as a child`
        THEN `no time limit: s 9(3), (5) and (6) do not apply to a claim for abuse as a child (s 9(9C))`
        ELSE `no day fixed yet: part 1 for a medical incident is due 12 months after the respondent answers my initial notice (s 9A(9)(b))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `ss 9(3), 9(9C), 9A(9)(b) -- the last day for part 1` `the route` `the respondent complied with s 9A(8)` `the day it complied` `the day of the incident` `symptoms were immediately apparent` `the day symptoms first appeared` `I instructed a law practice` `the day I first instructed it` `the day the respondent was identified` `I was under a legal disability` `the day the disability ended`
        `the earliest start` MEANS
            IF `the route` EQUALS `medical incident under s 9A`
            THEN `the day it complied`
            ELSE `the day of the incident`

@export Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim, and what follows (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 9(3), 9(5), 9(6), 9(9C), 9A(9))? Being late does not end the claim: the duty to give part 1 continues, and you must give a reasonable excuse for the delay. You are taken to have one if you made a health service complaint about the person in time and give part 1 as soon as practicable after the complaint is finalised. There is no time limit for a claim for abuse suffered as a child.
GIVEN `route` IS A `Part 1 route` @desc Your kind of claim: ordinary claim; abuse as a child (sexual abuse or serious physical abuse when you were under 18, or psychological abuse connected with it); or medical incident under s 9A
      `respondent answered initial notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Medical incident only: whether the respondent has given you its written response and documents under s 9A(8); otherwise answer either way
      `day respondent answered` IS A DATE @desc Medical incident only: the day it did so, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day of incident` IS A DATE @desc The day the incident that caused your injury happened, as an ISO date
      `symptoms immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the symptoms of your injury were immediately apparent when the incident happened
      `day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE @desc If they were not, the day the symptoms first appeared, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have instructed a law practice to act for you in seeking damages for this injury (a community legal service does not count)
      `day first instructed` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you first instructed it, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day respondent identified` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the person you propose to sue was identified, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under a legal disability as the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 means it (for example under 18) when the incident happened
      `day disability ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it ended, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day part 1 given` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave, or will give, part 1 of your notice of claim, as an ISO date
      `health complaint in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a health service complaint about the person to the Health Rights Commissioner or the Health Quality and Complaints Commission within the time for it, or to the health ombudsman within 2 years after you became aware of the matter
      `gave soon after complaint finalised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you give part 1 as soon as practicable after that complaint was finalised
GIVETH A `Was I late`
`Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` MEANS
    `ss 9(5), 9(6) -- was I late with part 1` `route` `respondent answered initial notice` `day respondent answered` `day of incident` `symptoms immediately apparent` `day symptoms first appeared` `instructed a law practice` `day first instructed` `day respondent identified` `legal disability` `day disability ended` `day part 1 given` `health complaint in time` `gave soon after complaint finalised`

GIVEN `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
      `symptoms were immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE
      `I instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I first instructed it` IS A DATE
      `the day the respondent was identified` IS A DATE
      `I was under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the disability ended` IS A DATE
      `the day given` IS A DATE
      `I made a health service complaint in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Was I late`
`ss 9A(6), 9A(6A) -- was I late with the initial notice` `the day of the incident` `symptoms were immediately apparent` `the day symptoms first appeared` `I instructed a law practice` `the day I first instructed it` `the day the respondent was identified` `I was under a legal disability` `the day the disability ended` `the day given` `I made a health service complaint in time` `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised` MEANS
    `ss 9(5), 9(6) -- what follows` (`given by the last day under` `s 9A(4), (6) -- give the initial notice in time, or with an excuse` `give my initial notice` `the day of the incident` `the last day` `the day given`) `I made a health service complaint in time` `I gave it as soon as practicable after the complaint was finalised`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `ss 9(3), 9A(4), 19 -- the last day` `the day of the incident` `symptoms were immediately apparent` `the day symptoms first appeared` `I instructed a law practice` `the day I first instructed it` `the day the respondent was identified` `I was under a legal disability` `the day the disability ended`

@export Am I late with my initial notice for a medical incident, and what follows (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 9A(4), 9A(6), 9A(6A))? Being late does not end the claim: the duty to give the initial notice continues, and you must give a reasonable excuse for the delay in it. You are taken to have one if you made a health service complaint about the person in time and give the notice as soon as practicable after the complaint is finalised.
GIVEN `day of medical incident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the medical incident, as an ISO date
      `symptoms immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the symptoms of your injury were immediately apparent
      `day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE @desc If they were not, the day the symptoms first appeared, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `instructed a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have instructed a law practice to act for you in seeking damages for this injury (a community legal service does not count)
      `day first instructed` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you first instructed it, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day respondent identified` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the person you propose to sue was identified, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under a legal disability as the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 means it (for example under 18) when the incident happened
      `day disability ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it ended, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day initial notice given` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave, or will give, the initial notice, as an ISO date
      `health complaint in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a health service complaint about the person to the Health Rights Commissioner or the Health Quality and Complaints Commission within the time for it, or to the health ombudsman within 2 years after you became aware of the matter
      `gave soon after complaint finalised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you give the initial notice as soon as practicable after that complaint was finalised
GIVETH A `Was I late`
`Am I late with my initial notice` MEANS
    `ss 9A(6), 9A(6A) -- was I late with the initial notice` `day of medical incident` `symptoms immediately apparent` `day symptoms first appeared` `instructed a law practice` `day first instructed` `day respondent identified` `legal disability` `day disability ended` `day initial notice given` `health complaint in time` `gave soon after complaint finalised`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 9(3A), 10, 13 -- by when I give part 2`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 9(3A) "Part 2 of the notice must be given ... within 2 months after the earlier of the following to happen-- (a) the
-- person to whom part 1 of the notice was given complies with section 10(1); (b) the person ... is, under section 13,
-- conclusively presumed to be satisfied part 1 of the notice is a complying part 1 notice of claim."
-- s 10(1): respond within the period prescribed by regulation "or, if no period is prescribed, within 1 month after
-- receiving part 1" (the fallback taken: fork F3). s 13: not responding within that period, the person is presumed
-- satisfied. The presumption is taken to arise on the day after the last day for a response (fork F6). A response given
-- late is not compliance with s 10(1).
GIVEN `the day part 1 was received` IS A DATE
      `the person responded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it responded` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(3A) -- the last day for part 2` `the day part 1 was received` `the person responded` `the day it responded` MEANS
    `the date` 2 `months after` `the trigger`
    WHERE
        `the last day to respond` MEANS `the date` 1 `months after` `the day part 1 was received`
        `the trigger` MEANS
            IF `the person responded` AND (NOT (`the day` `the day it responded` `is after` `the last day to respond`))
            THEN `the day it responded`
            ELSE `the day` 1 `days after` `the last day to respond`

@export By when must I give part 2 of my notice of claim (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 9(3A), 10(1), 13)? Within 2 months after the person you gave part 1 to responds under s 10(1) (it has 1 month after receiving part 1, unless a regulation sets another period), or, if it does not respond in that time, after it is presumed satisfied with part 1 (the day after its time to respond ends), whichever comes first.
GIVEN `day part 1 received` IS A DATE @desc The day the person received part 1 of your notice of claim, as an ISO date
      `person responded in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has responded to part 1 in writing under s 10(1) (accepting it is a proper respondent, asking for more information, or saying it is not a proper respondent)
      `day of response` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day of its response, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give part 2 of my notice of claim` MEANS
    `s 9(3A) -- the last day for part 2` `day part 1 received` `person responded in writing` `day of response`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 13, 18 -- whether I can go on with my claim after part 1`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 18(1) "A claimant's failure to give a complying part 1 notice of claim prevents the claimant from proceeding further
-- with the claim unless--" the respondent stated it is satisfied (or that I have remedied it), is presumed satisfied
-- (s 13), waived compliance, or the court declared it remedied or authorised me to proceed. "Unless" once met, and the
-- failure: the text's no ("prevents"). The court's orders may be on conditions (s 18(2)).
DECLARE `Can I go on` IS ONE OF
    `yes: my part 1 is a complying part 1 notice of claim`
    `yes: the respondent stated it is satisfied with part 1, or that I have taken reasonable action to remedy it (s 18(1)(a)(i))`
    `yes: the respondent did not respond in time and is conclusively presumed satisfied (s 13, s 18(1)(a)(ii))`
    `yes: the respondent waived compliance (s 18(1)(b))`
    `yes: the court declared that I remedied the noncompliance, or authorised me to proceed, on any conditions it set (s 18(1)(c), (2))`
    `no: my failure to give a complying part 1 notice prevents me from proceeding further with the claim (s 18(1))`

GIVEN `part 1 complies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent stated it is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent did not respond in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent waived compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court declared or authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I go on`
`s 18 -- can I go on` `part 1 complies` `the respondent stated it is satisfied` `the respondent did not respond in time` `the respondent waived compliance` `the court declared or authorised` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `part 1 complies`
        THEN `yes: my part 1 is a complying part 1 notice of claim`
        IF `the respondent stated it is satisfied`
        THEN `yes: the respondent stated it is satisfied with part 1, or that I have taken reasonable action to remedy it (s 18(1)(a)(i))`
        IF `the respondent did not respond in time`
        THEN `yes: the respondent did not respond in time and is conclusively presumed satisfied (s 13, s 18(1)(a)(ii))`
        IF `the respondent waived compliance`
        THEN `yes: the respondent waived compliance (s 18(1)(b))`
        IF `the court declared or authorised`
        THEN `yes: the court declared that I remedied the noncompliance, or authorised me to proceed, on any conditions it set (s 18(1)(c), (2))`
        OTHERWISE `no: my failure to give a complying part 1 notice prevents me from proceeding further with the claim (s 18(1))`

@export Can I go on with my claim if my part 1 notice of claim did not comply (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 13, 18)? A part 1 that does not comply stops the claim unless the respondent says it is satisfied (or that you have fixed it), is presumed satisfied because it did not respond in time, or waives compliance, or the court declares you have fixed it or lets you go on.
GIVEN `part 1 complies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your part 1 complied with s 9 (the approved form, the information and documents required, given in time or with a reasonable excuse)
      `respondent satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the respondent has stated in writing that it is satisfied with part 1, or that you have taken reasonable action to fix what was wrong
      `no response in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the respondent failed to respond to part 1 under s 10 or s 12 within its time (usually 1 month after receiving it)
      `respondent waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the respondent waived compliance with the requirement you did not meet
      `court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, on your application, declared that you remedied the noncompliance or authorised you to proceed despite it
GIVETH A `Can I go on`
`Can I go on with my claim after part 1` MEANS
    `s 18 -- can I go on` `part 1 complies` `respondent satisfied` `no response in time` `respondent waived` `court order`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `div 1A (ss 20B-20J) -- a child injured by medical treatment` -- arises only for a claim for a child's injury from medical treatment
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 20B: the division applies if the claimant is (or was when the cause of action arose) a child and the injury arose
-- out of medical treatment. s 20C(1): a parent or legal guardian "must give part 1 ... before the earlier of" (a) 6
-- years after the day the parent knew or ought reasonably to have known of the injury, (b) 18 months after the day the
-- parent first consults a practitioner about seeking damages (a community legal service disregarded, s 20C(4)).
-- "Before the earlier of the following days": the last day is the day before the earlier day (fork F7).
GIVEN `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
      `the parent consulted a practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the first consultation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 20C(1) -- the earlier day` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` `the parent consulted a practitioner` `the day of the first consultation` MEANS
    IF `the parent consulted a practitioner`
    THEN `the earlier of` (`the date` 72 `months after` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known`) `and` (`the date` 18 `months after` `the day of the first consultation`)
    ELSE `the date` 72 `months after` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known`

GIVEN `I am or was a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury arose out of medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
      `the parent consulted a practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the first consultation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 20C(1) -- the last day for my parent` `I am or was a child` `the injury arose out of medical treatment` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` `the parent consulted a practitioner` `the day of the first consultation` MEANS
    IF `I am or was a child` AND `the injury arose out of medical treatment`
    THEN JUST (`the day` (-1) `days after` (`s 20C(1) -- the earlier day` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` `the parent consulted a practitioner` `the day of the first consultation`))
    ELSE NOTHING

@export By when must my parent or guardian give part 1 of a notice of claim for my injury from medical treatment as a child (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 20B, 20C)? Before the earlier of 6 years after the parent knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the injury, and 18 months after the parent first consulted a lawyer about seeking damages. The answer is the last day. No answer if the injury did not arise from medical treatment of a child.
GIVEN `child claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a child (under 18), or were one when your cause of action arose
      `from medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury arose out of medical treatment given to you
      `day parent knew` IS A DATE @desc The day your parent or legal guardian knew, or ought reasonably to have known, that the injury had occurred, as an ISO date (whether they "ought to have known" earlier is for the court; give the day you take it to be)
      `parent consulted a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your parent or guardian has consulted a lawyer about seeking damages for the injury (a community legal service does not count)
      `day of first consultation` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day of the first such consultation, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must my parent give part 1 for my medical treatment injury` MEANS
    `s 20C(1) -- the last day for my parent` `child claimant` `from medical treatment` `day parent knew` `parent consulted a lawyer` `day of first consultation`

-- The rule: my parent MUST give part 1 WITHIN the days to the last day; LEST the respondent MAY apply for an order that
-- the claim not proceed (s 20D). Not a breach by the child: the late notice opens the respondent's application.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 20C(1), 20D -- my parent gives part 1 in time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `my parent or legal guardian`
    MUST `give part 1 of my notice of claim`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the respondent`
        MAY `apply to the court for an order that the claim not proceed`

-- s 20D, 20E, 20F: given late, the respondent may apply for the claim not to proceed; the court decides on the justice
-- of the case; if the application is dismissed, amounts for the parent's costs and gratuitous services before part 1
-- are not recoverable "unless the court orders otherwise". s 20H, 20I, 20J: if a notice of an adverse event was given
-- and part 1 is late, notice of the claim "can be given only with the leave of the court", the onus is on the claimant,
-- and the same amounts are not recoverable if leave is given, unless the court orders otherwise.
DECLARE `My parent's late notice` IS ONE OF
    `in time: my parent gives part 1 by the last day under s 20C`
    `late: the respondent may apply for an order that my claim not proceed (s 20D); the court decides on the justice of the case (s 20E); if the application is dismissed, I can not recover my parent's costs and gratuitous services for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise (s 20F)`
    `late after a notice of an adverse event: part 1 can be given only with the court's leave, and I must show why the claim should proceed (s 20H, 20I); if leave is given, I can not recover my parent's costs and gratuitous services for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise (s 20J)`
    `not covered: division 1A applies only to a claim for a child's injury from medical treatment (s 20B)`

GIVEN `I am or was a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury arose out of medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
      `the parent consulted a practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the first consultation` IS A DATE
      `the day part 1 was given` IS A DATE
      `a notice of an adverse event was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My parent's late notice`
`ss 20C-20J -- what follows a late notice for a child` `I am or was a child` `the injury arose out of medical treatment` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` `the parent consulted a practitioner` `the day of the first consultation` `the day part 1 was given` `a notice of an adverse event was given` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 20C(1) -- the last day for my parent` `I am or was a child` `the injury arose out of medical treatment` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` `the parent consulted a practitioner` `the day of the first consultation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: division 1A applies only to a claim for a child's injury from medical treatment (s 20B)`
    WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN
        IF `in time` `the last day`
        THEN `in time: my parent gives part 1 by the last day under s 20C`
        ELSE IF `a notice of an adverse event was given`
             THEN `late after a notice of an adverse event: part 1 can be given only with the court's leave, and I must show why the claim should proceed (s 20H, 20I); if leave is given, I can not recover my parent's costs and gratuitous services for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise (s 20J)`
             ELSE `late: the respondent may apply for an order that my claim not proceed (s 20D); the court decides on the justice of the case (s 20E); if the application is dismissed, I can not recover my parent's costs and gratuitous services for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise (s 20F)`
    WHERE
        `in time` `the last` MEANS
            IF `the day` `the day part 1 was given` `is before` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `the rule is met` (`s 20C(1), 20D -- my parent gives part 1 in time` (`the days from` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` `to` `the last`)) `my parent or legal guardian` `give part 1 of my notice of claim` (`the days from` `the day the parent knew or ought to have known` `to` `the day part 1 was given`)

@export What follows if my parent or guardian gave part 1 late for my injury from medical treatment as a child (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 20C-20J)? Late, the respondent may ask the court to stop the claim, and the court decides on the justice of the case. If the treating provider had given your parent a notice of an adverse event, a late part 1 needs the court's leave and you must show why the claim should go on. Either way you may lose the parent's costs and care for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise.
GIVEN `child claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a child (under 18), or were one when your cause of action arose
      `from medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury arose out of medical treatment given to you
      `day parent knew` IS A DATE @desc The day your parent or legal guardian knew, or ought reasonably to have known, that the injury had occurred, as an ISO date
      `parent consulted a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your parent or guardian has consulted a lawyer about seeking damages for the injury (a community legal service does not count)
      `day of first consultation` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day of the first such consultation, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day part 1 given` IS A DATE @desc The day your parent gave, or will give, part 1 of the notice of claim, as an ISO date
      `adverse event notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who treated you gave your parent or guardian a written notice of an adverse event arising out of the treatment (s 20G)
GIVETH A `My parent's late notice`
`What follows a late notice for my medical treatment injury as a child` MEANS
    `ss 20C-20J -- what follows a late notice for a child` `child claimant` `from medical treatment` `day parent knew` `parent consulted a lawyer` `day of first consultation` `day part 1 given` `adverse event notice`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 22 -- what I must give the respondent, and by when`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 22(5)(a) copies of reports I hold "within 1 month after giving notice of a claim", and of reports that come to me
-- later "within 7 days after they come into the claimant's possession"; s 22(5)(b) an answer to a request for
-- information "within 1 month after receiving it"; s 22(6) a change in my condition or circumstances "within 1 month
-- after becoming aware of the change". Each "within the period prescribed under a regulation or, if no period is
-- prescribed, ..." (the fallback taken: fork F3).
DECLARE `My disclosure duty` IS ONE OF
    `copies of reports and material I held when I gave notice of my claim`
    `a copy of a report or material that came into my possession later`
    `an answer to the respondent's request for information`
    `telling the respondent of a change in my condition or circumstances`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A `My disclosure duty`
      `the day it arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 22(5), (6) -- the last day` `the duty` `the day it arose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `a copy of a report or material that came into my possession later` THEN `the day` 7 `days after` `the day it arose`
    OTHERWISE `the date` 1 `months after` `the day it arose`

@export By when must I give the respondent my documents or information (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 22(5), (6))? Copies of reports you hold: 1 month after you gave notice of your claim; a report you get later: 7 days after you get it; an answer to the respondent's request for information: 1 month after you receive the request; a change in your condition or circumstances: 1 month after you become aware of it (unless a regulation sets other periods).
GIVEN `duty` IS A `My disclosure duty` @desc Which duty: copies of reports and material I held when I gave notice of my claim; a copy of a report or material that came into my possession later; an answer to the respondent's request for information; or telling the respondent of a change in my condition or circumstances
      `day it arose` IS A DATE @desc The day the time runs from: the day you gave notice of your claim; the day the later report came into your possession; the day you received the request; or the day you became aware of the change; as an ISO date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give the respondent documents or information` MEANS
    `s 22(5), (6) -- the last day` `duty` `day it arose`

-- The rule: I MUST give the documents or information WITHIN the days allowed; LEST a breach (the consequences below).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 22 -- give the documents or information` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    MUST `give the documents or information`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "the claimant did not give the respondent the documents or information within the time in s 22(5) or (6)"

-- s 22(8) "If a claimant fails, without proper reason, to comply fully with a request by a respondent under this
-- section, the claimant is liable for costs to the respondent resulting from the failure." It speaks of a "request":
-- read as reaching only the duties that answer a request (s 22(1)(b), (2)), not the copies of s 22(1)(a) nor the change
-- of s 22(6) (fork F8). s 32: a document a party fails to disclose "can not be used by the party" in a later
-- proceeding "unless the court orders otherwise" (the copies duties). s 35: the court may order a party in default to
-- remedy it, with costs.
DECLARE `If I miss the time` IS ONE OF
    `in time: nothing follows`
    `late, without proper reason: I am liable for the respondent's costs resulting from the failure (s 22(8)), and the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
    `late, with a proper reason: no liability for costs under s 22(8), but the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
    `late: the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35), and I can not use an undisclosed document in a later court proceeding unless the court orders otherwise (s 32)`
    `late: the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A `My disclosure duty`
      `the day it arose` IS A DATE
      `I gave it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `I had a proper reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `If I miss the time`
`ss 22(8), 32, 35 -- if I miss the time` `the duty` `the day it arose` `I gave it` `the day I gave it` `the day asked about` `I had a proper reason` MEANS
    IF `in time`
    THEN `in time: nothing follows`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the duty`
         WHEN `an answer to the respondent's request for information` THEN
             IF `I had a proper reason`
             THEN `late, with a proper reason: no liability for costs under s 22(8), but the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
             ELSE `late, without proper reason: I am liable for the respondent's costs resulting from the failure (s 22(8)), and the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
         WHEN `telling the respondent of a change in my condition or circumstances` THEN `late: the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
         OTHERWISE `late: the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35), and I can not use an undisclosed document in a later court proceeding unless the court orders otherwise (s 32)`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day it arose` `to` (`s 22(5), (6) -- the last day` `the duty` `the day it arose`)
        `the time done` MEANS
            IF `I gave it`
            THEN `the days from` `the day it arose` `to` `the day I gave it`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day it arose` `to` `the day asked about`
        `in time` MEANS
            IF `I gave it`
            THEN `the rule is met` (`s 22 -- give the documents or information` `the days allowed`) `I` `give the documents or information` `the time done`
            ELSE NOT (`the day` `the day asked about` `is after` (`s 22(5), (6) -- the last day` `the duty` `the day it arose`))

@export What follows if I do not give the respondent my documents or information in time (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 22(8), 32, 35)? If you fail without proper reason to answer the respondent's request, you are liable for the respondent's costs caused by it. A document you fail to disclose can not be used by you in court unless the court orders otherwise. The court may order you to remedy any default, with costs.
GIVEN `duty` IS A `My disclosure duty` @desc Which duty: copies of reports and material I held when I gave notice of my claim; a copy of a report or material that came into my possession later; an answer to the respondent's request for information; or telling the respondent of a change in my condition or circumstances
      `day it arose` IS A DATE @desc The day the time runs from (the day you gave notice, got the later report, received the request, or became aware of the change), as an ISO date
      `given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given it
      `day given` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you gave it, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day asked about` IS A DATE @desc If not, the day you are asking about (for example today), as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `proper reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a proper reason for not complying fully (for the court to decide; answer as you understand it)
GIVETH A `If I miss the time`
`What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` MEANS
    `ss 22(8), 32, 35 -- if I miss the time` `duty` `day it arose` `given` `day given` `day asked about` `proper reason`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 23-25 -- expert reports and examinations`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 25: if the respondent wants an expert report and "fails to obtain the claimant's agreement", the claimant "must
-- comply with a request ... to undergo, at the respondent's expense" a medical examination (or capacity assessment) by
-- a doctor or expert the claimant selects "from a panel of at least 3" (2 if 3 are not available, s 25(4)); "However, a
-- claimant is not obliged ... if it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious" (s 25(3), a judgment: asked).
DECLARE `Must I be examined` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must undergo the examination or assessment, with a doctor or expert I select from the respondent's panel, at the respondent's expense (s 25(2))`
    `no: I am not obliged, because it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious (s 25(3))`
    `no: the request does not meet s 25(2): it must be at the respondent's expense and let me choose from a panel of at least 3 (or 2, if 3 suitable doctors or experts are not available)`
    `not this section: I agreed to an expert report, so it is a joint arrangement under s 23`

GIVEN `I agreed to the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the respondent's expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the panel size` IS A NUMBER
      `3 were available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I may select from the panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Must I be examined`
`s 25 -- must I be examined` `I agreed to the report` `at the respondent's expense` `the panel size` `3 were available` `I may select from the panel` `it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I agreed to the report`
        THEN `not this section: I agreed to an expert report, so it is a joint arrangement under s 23`
        IF NOT (`at the respondent's expense` AND `I may select from the panel` AND `the panel is big enough`)
        THEN `no: the request does not meet s 25(2): it must be at the respondent's expense and let me choose from a panel of at least 3 (or 2, if 3 suitable doctors or experts are not available)`
        IF `it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious`
        THEN `no: I am not obliged, because it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious (s 25(3))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I must undergo the examination or assessment, with a doctor or expert I select from the respondent's panel, at the respondent's expense (s 25(2))`
    WHERE
        `the panel is big enough` MEANS
            IF `3 were available` THEN `the panel size` AT LEAST 3 ELSE `the panel size` AT LEAST 2

@export Must I go to the medical examination or capacity assessment the respondent asks for (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 25)? If you have not agreed to a joint expert report, you must, if the respondent pays and lets you choose the doctor or expert from a panel of at least 3 (2 if 3 suitable are not available). You need not if it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious.
GIVEN `agreed to report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed with the respondent to arrange an expert report jointly (s 23)
      `respondent pays` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the examination or assessment is at the respondent's expense
      `panel size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many doctors or experts the respondent nominated on the panel in its request
      `three available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether 3 doctors or experts with suitable qualifications and experience in the field were available for the panel
      `I select` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request lets you select the doctor or expert from the panel
      `unreasonable or repetitious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the examination is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious (for example you have had the same examination already); for the court in the end, answer as you understand it
GIVETH A `Must I be examined`
`Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` MEANS
    `s 25 -- must I be examined` `agreed to report` `respondent pays` `panel size` `three available` `I select` `unreasonable or repetitious`

-- s 24: "If an expert report is obtained by agreement ... and the claimant is liable for the cost ..., the respondent
-- must, at the claimant's request, reimburse the claimant for the reasonable cost"; "subject to the terms of any
-- agreement" (s 24(2)). The "if" unmet: no right under s 24 (JUST FALSE kind).
DECLARE `Reimbursement` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the respondent must reimburse my reasonable cost of the report, on my request (s 24(1))`
    `as our agreement says: my right is subject to its terms, and they deal with the cost (s 24(2))`
    `no: s 24 gives no right unless the report was obtained by agreement, I am liable for its cost, and I ask (s 24(1))`

GIVEN `obtained by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am liable for the cost` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I asked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `our agreement deals with the cost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reimbursement`
`s 24 -- reimbursement` `obtained by agreement` `I am liable for the cost` `I asked` `our agreement deals with the cost` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`obtained by agreement` AND `I am liable for the cost` AND `I asked`)
        THEN `no: s 24 gives no right unless the report was obtained by agreement, I am liable for its cost, and I ask (s 24(1))`
        IF `our agreement deals with the cost`
        THEN `as our agreement says: my right is subject to its terms, and they deal with the cost (s 24(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the respondent must reimburse my reasonable cost of the report, on my request (s 24(1))`

@export Must the respondent pay me back for an expert report we arranged together (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 24)? If the report was obtained by agreement and you are liable for its cost, the respondent must reimburse your reasonable cost when you ask, subject to the terms of any agreement between you.
GIVEN `by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the expert report was obtained by agreement between you and the respondent (s 23)
      `I am liable for cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are liable for the cost of obtaining the report
      `I asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked the respondent to reimburse you
      `agreement deals with cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your agreement with the respondent has terms about who bears the cost of the report
GIVETH A `Reimbursement`
`Must the respondent reimburse my expert report` MEANS
    `s 24 -- reimbursement` `by agreement` `I am liable for cost` `I asked` `agreement deals with cost`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 20, 27, 29A -- what the respondent must give me, and by when`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 27(2)(a) copies "within 1 month after receiving a complying part 1 notice of claim", later material "within 7 days
-- after it comes into the respondent's possession"; s 27(2)(b) an answer to my request "within 1 month after receiving
-- it" (each subject to a regulation: fork F3). s 29A(5): where copies over 200 pages were offered for inspection and I
-- require copies, "1 month after the requirement" if not over 200 pages, "otherwise-- 1 month after payment by the other
-- person of an amount of 50c for each page the total number of pages exceeds 200 pages". s 20(1): within 6 months after
-- receiving a complying part 1 notice of claim (or the day s 20(2) treats it as given), the respondent must tell me
-- whether liability is admitted and make an offer or counter offer, or settle by accepting mine.
DECLARE `The respondent's duty` IS ONE OF
    `copies of the reports and material it holds`
    `a copy of a report or material it gets later`
    `an answer to my request for information about the incident`
    `copies I required after inspecting more than 200 pages, where the copies are 200 pages or fewer`
    `copies I required after inspecting more than 200 pages, where the copies are more than 200 pages`
    `its notice about liability and its offer of settlement (s 20(1))`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A `The respondent's duty`
      `the day it arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 20(1), 27(2), 29A(5) -- the respondent's last day` `the duty` `the day it arose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `a copy of a report or material it gets later` THEN `the day` 7 `days after` `the day it arose`
    WHEN `its notice about liability and its offer of settlement (s 20(1))` THEN `the date` 6 `months after` `the day it arose`
    OTHERWISE `the date` 1 `months after` `the day it arose`

@export By when must the respondent give me documents, information, or its answer on liability and its offer (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 20(1), 27(2), 29A(5))? Copies of reports it holds: 1 month after it received your complying part 1; later material: 7 days after it gets it; an answer to your request for information: 1 month after the request; copies you required after inspecting a large set: 1 month after you required them, or, over 200 pages, 1 month after you paid 50c a page over 200; its notice on liability and its offer: 6 months after it received your complying part 1.
GIVEN `duty` IS A `The respondent's duty` @desc Which duty of the respondent: copies of the reports and material it holds; a copy of a report or material it gets later; an answer to my request for information about the incident; copies I required after inspecting more than 200 pages, where the copies are 200 pages or fewer; the same where the copies are more than 200 pages; or its notice about liability and its offer of settlement
      `day it arose` IS A DATE @desc The day the respondent's time runs from: the day it received your complying part 1 (or waived the defects, or the court ruled); the day it got the later material; the day it received your request; the day you required the copies; or, over 200 pages, the day you paid for them; as an ISO date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the respondent give me documents or its offer` MEANS
    `ss 20(1), 27(2), 29A(5) -- the respondent's last day` `duty` `day it arose`

-- s 29A(5)(b) "an amount of 50c for each page the total number of pages exceeds 200 pages". Nothing for 200 pages or
-- fewer (s 29A(5)(a)).
GIVEN `the pages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 29A(5) -- the amount for the pages` `the pages` MEANS
    IF `the pages` GREATER THAN 200
    THEN (`the pages` MINUS 200) TIMES 0.5
    ELSE 0

@export How much must I pay to get copies of more than 200 pages from the respondent (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 29A(5))? Where the documents total more than 200 pages, the respondent may offer you inspection instead of copies. If you then require copies of more than 200 pages, it must give them within 1 month after you pay 50 cents for each page over 200. The answer is in dollars.
GIVEN `pages` IS A NUMBER @desc The total number of pages of the copies you require
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must I pay for copies over 200 pages` MEANS
    `s 29A(5) -- the amount for the pages` `pages`

-- s 20(4): a claimant to whom a written offer or counter offer is made "must ... respond in writing to the offer within
-- the period prescribed under a regulation or, if no period is prescribed, within 3 months after receiving it,
-- indicating acceptance or rejection" (fallback taken: fork F3).
@export By when must I answer a written settlement offer from the respondent (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 20(4))? Within 3 months after you receive it, accepting or rejecting it in writing (unless a regulation sets another period).
GIVEN `day offer received` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the respondent's written offer or counter offer of settlement, as an ISO date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I answer a settlement offer` MEANS
    `the date` 3 `months after` `day offer received`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 36-40 -- the compulsory conference and mandatory final offers`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 36(2)(b), (3): any party may call the conference at a reasonable time and place it nominates "if the relevant day
-- has passed": the later of (a) 6 months after I gave a complying part 1 notice (with more than 1 respondent, 6 months
-- after I last gave a respondent part 1 under s 14(1)), (b) if a person gave notice under s 12 that it is a proper
-- respondent, 6 months after it gave notice ("or, if there is more than 1 person ..., the day 6 months after the day
-- after the last person gives notice"). "Has passed": from the day after the relevant day (fork F9).
GIVEN `the day counted for (a)` IS A DATE
      `a proper respondent notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the last such notice` IS A DATE
      `there is more than 1 such person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 36(3) -- the relevant day` `the day counted for (a)` `a proper respondent notice was given` `the day of the last such notice` `there is more than 1 such person` MEANS
    IF `a proper respondent notice was given`
    THEN `the later of` (`the date` 6 `months after` `the day counted for (a)`) `and` `the day for (b)`
    ELSE `the date` 6 `months after` `the day counted for (a)`
    WHERE
        `the day for (b)` MEANS
            IF `there is more than 1 such person`
            THEN `the date` 6 `months after` (`the day` 1 `days after` `the day of the last such notice`)
            ELSE `the date` 6 `months after` `the day of the last such notice`

@export From when may I call the compulsory conference myself, at a time and place I nominate (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 36(2), (3))? Once the relevant day has passed: the later of 6 months after you gave a complying part 1 notice (with several respondents, after you last gave one part 1) and 6 months after the respondent told you it is a proper respondent. Before that, the conference is held at a time and place the parties agree. The answer is the first day you may call it.
GIVEN `day part 1 given` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the respondent a complying part 1 notice of claim; with more than 1 respondent, the day you last gave a respondent part 1 under s 14(1); as an ISO date
      `proper respondent notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person you gave part 1 to has given you notice under s 12 that it is a proper respondent to your claim
      `day of last notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the (last) such person gave notice, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `more than one such person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave part 1 to more than 1 person
GIVETH A DATE
`From when may I call the compulsory conference` MEANS
    `the day` 1 `days after` (`s 36(3) -- the relevant day` `day part 1 given` `proper respondent notice` `day of last notice` `more than one such person`)

-- s 37(1) "At least 7 days before the compulsory conference is held, each party must give each other party" the
-- documents, the signed statement, details of legal representation and a certificate of readiness. Read as: on or
-- before the day 7 days before the conference (fork F10).
@export By when must I give the other parties my documents, statement and certificate of readiness before the compulsory conference (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 37(1))? At least 7 days before the conference is held. The answer is the last day.
GIVEN `day of conference` IS A DATE @desc The day the compulsory conference is to be held, as an ISO date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give my material before the conference` MEANS
    `the day` (-7) `days after` `day of conference`

-- s 39(1): if not settled at the conference, the claimant and a respondent "must, unless the court has dispensed with
-- this obligation, exchange written final offers-- (a) at the conference; or (b) if the conference has been dispensed
-- with, within 14 days after the date of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference." s 40(9) the court may
-- dispense with them: then no day (NOTHING).
GIVEN `the conference was dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the conference or of the dispensation` IS A DATE
      `the court dispensed with final offers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 39(1) -- the last day for final offers` `the conference was dispensed with` `the day of the conference or of the dispensation` `the court dispensed with final offers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court dispensed with final offers`
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the conference was dispensed with`
        THEN JUST (`the day` 14 `days after` `the day of the conference or of the dispensation`)
        OTHERWISE JUST `the day of the conference or of the dispensation`

@export By when must I exchange my mandatory final offer with the respondent (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 39(1), 40(9))? If the claim does not settle at the compulsory conference, at the conference; if the conference was dispensed with, within 14 days after the agreement or order dispensing with it. No answer if the court dispensed with final offers.
GIVEN `conference dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the compulsory conference was dispensed with, by the parties' agreement or by the court
      `day of conference or dispensation` IS A DATE @desc The day of the conference; or, if it was dispensed with, the date of the agreement or order dispensing with it; as an ISO date
      `final offers dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has dispensed with the obligation to make mandatory final offers
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I exchange my mandatory final offer` MEANS
    `s 39(1) -- the last day for final offers` `conference dispensed with` `day of conference or dispensation` `final offers dispensed with`

-- s 40(4) "A mandatory final offer must remain open for 14 days and a proceeding in a court based on a claim must not
-- be started while the offer remains open." The rule: I SHANT start my proceeding WITHIN 14 days of the offer (the day
-- of the offer is day 0; the offer is open through day 14: fork F11).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 40(4) -- not while the offer is open` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    SHANT `start my court proceeding`
    WITHIN 14

DECLARE `Starting after the final offers` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the final offers are no longer open, so s 40(4) does not stop me`
    `no: a mandatory final offer is still open, and a proceeding must not be started while it is (s 40(4))`

GIVEN `the day of the offers` IS A DATE
      `the day I start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Starting after the final offers`
`s 40(4) -- may I start on this day` `the day of the offers` `the day I start` MEANS
    IF `the rule is met` `s 40(4) -- not while the offer is open` `I` `start my court proceeding` (`the days from` `the day of the offers` `to` `the day I start`)
    THEN `yes: the final offers are no longer open, so s 40(4) does not stop me`
    ELSE `no: a mandatory final offer is still open, and a proceeding must not be started while it is (s 40(4))`

@export May I start my court proceeding on this day, as far as the mandatory final offers go (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 40(4))? A mandatory final offer stays open for 14 days, and no proceeding may be started while it is open. Counting the day the offers were exchanged as day 0, the first day you may start is day 15.
GIVEN `day offers exchanged` IS A DATE @desc The day the mandatory final offers were made or exchanged (the later one, if on different days), as an ISO date
      `day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you propose to start your court proceeding, as an ISO date
GIVETH A `Starting after the final offers`
`May I start my proceeding after the final offers` MEANS
    `s 40(4) -- may I start on this day` `day offers exchanged` `day I start`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 42 -- by when I should start my court proceeding`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 42(1) "should be started-- (a) within 60 days after the conclusion of the compulsory conference; or (b) within a
-- further period" agreed or fixed by the court on my application within the 60 days. s 42(2) if the conference was
-- dispensed with: 60 days after the later of 6 months after I gave a complying part 1 notice (or last gave part 1 under
-- s 14(1)) and the date of the dispensation. s 42(3) if the court dispensed with final offers: a period the court fixes
-- (asked as the further period).
GIVEN `the conference was dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with` IS A DATE
      `the day part 1 was given` IS A DATE
      `a further period was agreed or fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 42(1)-(3) -- the day I should start by` `the conference was dispensed with` `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with` `the day part 1 was given` `a further period was agreed or fixed` `the last day of the further period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a further period was agreed or fixed`
        THEN `the last day of the further period`
        IF `the conference was dispensed with`
        THEN `the day` 60 `days after` (`the later of` (`the date` 6 `months after` `the day part 1 was given`) `and` `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with`)
        OTHERWISE `the day` 60 `days after` `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with`

@export By when should I start my court proceeding (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 42(1)-(3))? Within 60 days after the compulsory conference ends; if the conference was dispensed with, within 60 days after the later of 6 months after you gave a complying part 1 notice and the date it was dispensed with; or within a further period the parties agreed, or the court fixed, within those 60 days (or a period the court fixed when it dispensed with final offers).
GIVEN `conference dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the compulsory conference was dispensed with, by the parties' agreement or by the court
      `day conference ended or dispensed` IS A DATE @desc The day the compulsory conference concluded; or, if it was dispensed with, the date of the agreement or order dispensing with it; as an ISO date
      `day part 1 given` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the respondent a complying part 1 notice of claim (with several respondents, the day you last gave one part 1 under s 14(1)), as an ISO date
      `further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed, or the court fixed on your application, a further period to start (within the 60 days), or the court fixed a period when it dispensed with final offers
      `last day of further period` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of that further period, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when should I start my court proceeding` MEANS
    `s 42(1)-(3) -- the day I should start by` `conference dispensed with` `day conference ended or dispensed` `day part 1 given` `further period` `last day of further period`

-- The rule: I DO start my proceeding WITHIN the days to that day; LEST (not a bar: s 42(4)) the court may order costs of
-- the delay and fix a time limit. It is a "should", not a "must": the BREACH marks only that the time was not met.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 42 -- start within the time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `start my court proceeding`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "the proceeding was not started within the time in s 42(1), (2) or (3); s 42(4) lets the court order costs of the delay and fix a time limit"

-- s 42(4) "The expiry of the time ... does not prevent the claimant from starting the proceeding but the court may--
-- (a) unless the claimant establishes a reasonable excuse for the delay, order the claimant to pay ... a respondent's
-- costs arising out of the delay; and (b) on a respondent's application, make an order fixing a time limit". s 42(5)
-- "If the claimant fails to start the proceeding within a time limit fixed under subsection (4)(b), the claim is
-- barred", despite the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (s 42(6)).
DECLARE `Starting late` IS ONE OF
    `in time: I start within the time in s 42`
    `late, but not prevented: the court may order me to pay the respondent's costs of the delay, unless I establish a reasonable excuse, and may fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4))`
    `late, but not prevented: I have a reasonable excuse, so no costs order for the delay under s 42(4)(a); the court may still fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4)(b))`
    `barred: I did not start within the time limit the court fixed under s 42(4)(b) (s 42(5)), despite the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (s 42(6))`

GIVEN `the conference was dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with` IS A DATE
      `the day part 1 was given` IS A DATE
      `a further period was agreed or fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further period` IS A DATE
      `the day I start` IS A DATE
      `the court fixed a time limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the time limit` IS A DATE
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Starting late`
`s 42(4), (5) -- starting late` `the conference was dispensed with` `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with` `the day part 1 was given` `a further period was agreed or fixed` `the last day of the further period` `the day I start` `the court fixed a time limit` `the last day of the time limit` `I have a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `in time`
        THEN `in time: I start within the time in s 42`
        IF `the court fixed a time limit` AND (`the day` `the day I start` `is after` `the last day of the time limit`)
        THEN `barred: I did not start within the time limit the court fixed under s 42(4)(b) (s 42(5)), despite the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (s 42(6))`
        IF `I have a reasonable excuse`
        THEN `late, but not prevented: I have a reasonable excuse, so no costs order for the delay under s 42(4)(a); the court may still fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `late, but not prevented: the court may order me to pay the respondent's costs of the delay, unless I establish a reasonable excuse, and may fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4))`
    WHERE
        `the day it runs from` MEANS `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with`
        `the last day` MEANS `s 42(1)-(3) -- the day I should start by` `the conference was dispensed with` `the day the conference concluded or was dispensed with` `the day part 1 was given` `a further period was agreed or fixed` `the last day of the further period`
        `in time` MEANS
            IF `the day` `the day I start` `is before` `the day it runs from`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `the rule is met` (`s 42 -- start within the time` (`the days from` `the day it runs from` `to` `the last day`)) `I` `start my court proceeding` (`the days from` `the day it runs from` `to` `the day I start`)

@export What happens if I start my court proceeding after the time in s 42 (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 42(4)-(6))? Starting late is not barred, but the court may order you to pay the respondent's costs of the delay unless you show a reasonable excuse, and may fix a time limit on the respondent's application. If you miss a time limit the court fixed, the claim is barred, whatever the limitation period.
GIVEN `conference dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the compulsory conference was dispensed with, by the parties' agreement or by the court
      `day conference ended or dispensed` IS A DATE @desc The day the compulsory conference concluded; or, if it was dispensed with, the date of the agreement or order dispensing with it; as an ISO date
      `day part 1 given` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the respondent a complying part 1 notice of claim (with several respondents, the day you last gave one part 1 under s 14(1)), as an ISO date
      `further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed, or the court fixed, a further period to start (or the court fixed a period when it dispensed with final offers)
      `last day of further period` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of that further period, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you started, or propose to start, your court proceeding, as an ISO date
      `court fixed a time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, on a respondent's application, has fixed a time limit within which you must start (s 42(4)(b))
      `last day of time limit` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of that time limit, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can establish a reasonable excuse for the delay (for the court to decide; answer as you understand it)
GIVETH A `Starting late`
`What happens if I start my proceeding late` MEANS
    `s 42(4), (5) -- starting late` `conference dispensed with` `day conference ended or dispensed` `day part 1 given` `further period` `last day of further period` `day I start` `court fixed a time limit` `last day of time limit` `reasonable excuse`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 43, 44 -- starting an urgent proceeding` -- arises only where I need to start in court before finishing the steps
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 43: the court "may give leave" if satisfied there is an urgent need (asked); the proceeding "is stayed until the
-- claimant complies with this part" (s 43(3)), unless the court is satisfied I have a terminal condition and the trial
-- should be expedited and orders priority and certifies it for speedy trial (s 43(4)); then Part 1 (other than s 43),
-- ss 48, 56 and 59 and chapter 4 do not apply (s 43(5)). s 44: if each proposed respondent agrees, "the claimant may
-- start the proceeding" and it "is stayed until the claimant complies with this part" (s 44(8)).
DECLARE `Urgent start` IS ONE OF
    `yes, with the court's leave, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 or it ends (s 43(3))`
    `yes, with the court's leave, and it is not stayed: Part 1 (other than s 43), ss 48, 56 and 59 and chapter 4 no longer apply to my injury (s 43(4), (5))`
    `yes, because every proposed respondent agreed, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 or it ends (s 44(8))`
    `no: without the court's leave or every proposed respondent's agreement, I must first give notice of my claim and hold the compulsory conference (s 9(1), s 36(1))`

GIVEN `the court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court ordered a speedy trial for my terminal condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every proposed respondent agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Urgent start`
`ss 43, 44 -- urgent start` `the court gave leave` `the court ordered a speedy trial for my terminal condition` `every proposed respondent agreed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court gave leave` AND `the court ordered a speedy trial for my terminal condition`
        THEN `yes, with the court's leave, and it is not stayed: Part 1 (other than s 43), ss 48, 56 and 59 and chapter 4 no longer apply to my injury (s 43(4), (5))`
        IF `the court gave leave`
        THEN `yes, with the court's leave, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 or it ends (s 43(3))`
        IF `every proposed respondent agreed`
        THEN `yes, because every proposed respondent agreed, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 or it ends (s 44(8))`
        OTHERWISE `no: without the court's leave or every proposed respondent's agreement, I must first give notice of my claim and hold the compulsory conference (s 9(1), s 36(1))`

@export Can I start my court proceeding urgently, before finishing the pre-court steps (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 43, 44)? With the court's leave (if it is satisfied of an urgent need), or if every person you propose to sue agrees to your request in your notice of claim. Either way the proceeding is put on hold until you complete the steps, unless the court is satisfied you have a terminal condition and orders a speedy trial.
GIVEN `court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, satisfied there is an urgent need, has given you leave to start the proceeding despite not completing the pre-court steps
      `speedy trial for terminal condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, satisfied you have a terminal condition and the trial should be expedited, ordered the proceeding be given priority and certified it for speedy trial
      `all respondents agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every person you propose to sue agreed, in the approved form, to let you start despite not completing the steps (after you asked in your notice of claim)
GIVETH A `Urgent start`
`Can I start my proceeding urgently` MEANS
    `ss 43, 44 -- urgent start` `court gave leave` `speedy trial for terminal condition` `all respondents agreed`

-- s 44(7) "The advice must be given to the claimant before the end of 7 days after the proposed respondent receives
-- the notice of claim signed by the claimant's lawyer."
@export By when must the person I propose to sue tell me whether it agrees to my urgent proceeding (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 44(6), (7))? Before the end of 7 days after it receives your notice of claim signed by your lawyer. The answer is the last day.
GIVEN `day notice received` IS A DATE @desc The day the person received your notice of claim (signed by your lawyer) asking it to agree to an urgent proceeding, as an ISO date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the respondent answer my urgent request` MEANS
    `the day` 7 `days after` `day notice received`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 59 -- starting after the limitation period` -- arises only where the limitation period has ended or is close
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 59(1) "If a complying part 1 notice of claim is given before the end of the period of limitation applying to the
-- claim, the claimant may start a proceeding ... even though the period of limitation has ended." (2) only if started
-- within "(a) 6 months after the complying part 1 notice is given or leave to start the proceeding is granted; or (b) a
-- longer period allowed by the court." (3) if started without having complied with part 1, it is stayed. The period of
-- limitation (Limitation of Actions Act 1974, as extended under its part 3, s 59(4)) is asked. "Or leave is granted":
-- read as 6 months after the leave, where leave was granted (fork F12).
DECLARE `After the limitation period` IS ONE OF
    `the limitation period has not ended when I start: s 59 is not needed`
    `yes: my complying part 1 notice was given before the limitation period ended, and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
    `yes, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 (s 59(3)): my complying part 1 was given in time and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
    `no: s 59 does not help, because my complying part 1 notice was not given before the limitation period ended`
    `no: I start after the time s 59(2) allows (6 months after part 1 or leave, or the longer period the court allowed)`

GIVEN `the day the limitation period ends` IS A DATE
      `the day part 1 was given` IS A DATE
      `leave was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day leave was granted` IS A DATE
      `the court allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 59(2) -- the last day` `the day the limitation period ends` `the day part 1 was given` `leave was granted` `the day leave was granted` `the court allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period` MEANS
    IF `the court allowed a longer period` AND (`the day` `the last day of the longer period` `is after` `six months on`)
    THEN `the last day of the longer period`
    ELSE `six months on`
    WHERE
        `six months on` MEANS
            IF `leave was granted`
            THEN `the date` 6 `months after` `the day leave was granted`
            ELSE `the date` 6 `months after` `the day part 1 was given`

GIVEN `the day the limitation period ends` IS A DATE
      `the day part 1 was given` IS A DATE
      `leave was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day leave was granted` IS A DATE
      `the court allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE
      `I have complied with Part 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `After the limitation period`
`s 59 -- after the limitation period` `the day the limitation period ends` `the day part 1 was given` `leave was granted` `the day leave was granted` `the court allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period` `I have complied with Part 1` `the day I start` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the day` `the day I start` `is after` `the day the limitation period ends`)
        THEN `the limitation period has not ended when I start: s 59 is not needed`
        IF `the day` `the day part 1 was given` `is after` `the day the limitation period ends`
        THEN `no: s 59 does not help, because my complying part 1 notice was not given before the limitation period ended`
        IF `the day` `the day I start` `is after` (`s 59(2) -- the last day` `the day the limitation period ends` `the day part 1 was given` `leave was granted` `the day leave was granted` `the court allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period`)
        THEN `no: I start after the time s 59(2) allows (6 months after part 1 or leave, or the longer period the court allowed)`
        IF `I have complied with Part 1`
        THEN `yes: my complying part 1 notice was given before the limitation period ended, and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
        OTHERWISE `yes, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 (s 59(3)): my complying part 1 was given in time and I start within the time in s 59(2)`

@export Can I start my court proceeding after the limitation period has ended (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 59)? Yes, if you gave a complying part 1 notice of claim before the limitation period ended, and you start within 6 months after giving it (or after the court gave leave to start), or within a longer period the court allows. If you have not finished the pre-court steps, the proceeding is put on hold until you do.
GIVEN `day limitation period ends` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the limitation period for your claim under the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (usually 3 years after the injury), as extended under its part 3 if it was, as an ISO date
      `day part 1 given` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave a complying part 1 notice of claim, as an ISO date
      `leave granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has granted leave to start the proceeding
      `day leave granted` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was granted, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `longer period allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has allowed a longer period to start
      `last day of longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of that period, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `complied with Part 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have completed the pre-court steps in Part 1 (notice of claim, disclosure, compulsory conference and final offers, or their dispensation)
      `day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you start, or propose to start, the proceeding, as an ISO date
GIVETH A `After the limitation period`
`Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` MEANS
    `s 59 -- after the limitation period` `day limitation period ends` `day part 1 given` `leave granted` `day leave granted` `longer period allowed` `last day of longer period` `complied with Part 1` `day I start`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 6(4), 43(5), 56 -- costs when the court awards no more than the upper offer limit` -- arises only after judgment
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 56(2): an award at or below the lower offer limit: (a) less than my mandatory final offer but more than the
-- respondent's, no costs; (b) equal to or more than mine, costs to me on an indemnity basis from the day the proceeding
-- started, none before; (c) equal to or less than the respondent's, costs to the respondent on a standard basis from the
-- day the proceeding started, none before. s 56(3): above the lower and not above the upper offer limit: (a) costs to me
-- on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit; (b) to me, standard up to the declared costs limit before the
-- start, indemnity from it; (c) to me, standard up to the declared costs limit before the start, to the respondent,
-- standard from it. s 56(1): not for an award above the upper offer limit, nor appeals. s 6(4): ss 40(2) and 56 do not
-- apply to an unlawful intentional act done with intent to cause injury, or unlawful sexual assault or misconduct;
-- s 43(5)(b): nor to an urgent proceeding not stayed. Where my offer is not above the respondent's, an award can meet
-- both (b) and (c); (b) is taken (fork F13). The limits are fixed by the Minister's notice under s 75A (not deposited):
-- asked.
DECLARE `Costs under s 56` IS ONE OF
    `no costs are awarded either way (s 56(2)(a))`
    `costs to me on an indemnity basis from the day the proceeding started, and none before it (s 56(2)(b))`
    `costs to the respondent on a standard basis from the day the proceeding started, and none before it (s 56(2)(c))`
    `costs to me on a standard basis, up to the declared costs limit (s 56(3)(a))`
    `costs to me on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before the proceeding started, and on an indemnity basis from that day (s 56(3)(b))`
    `costs to me on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before the proceeding started, and to the respondent on a standard basis from that day (s 56(3)(c))`
    `s 56 does not apply: the award is more than the upper offer limit (s 56(1))`
    `s 56 does not apply: the injury came from an unlawful intentional act done to cause injury, or unlawful sexual assault or misconduct (s 6(4))`
    `s 56 does not apply: my urgent proceeding was not stayed (s 43(5)(b))`

GIVEN `the award` IS A NUMBER
      `the lower offer limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the upper offer limit` IS A NUMBER
      `my final offer` IS A NUMBER
      `the respondent's final offer` IS A NUMBER
      `an intentional or sexual wrong` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an urgent proceeding not stayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Costs under s 56`
`s 56 -- costs` `the award` `the lower offer limit` `the upper offer limit` `my final offer` `the respondent's final offer` `an intentional or sexual wrong` `an urgent proceeding not stayed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an intentional or sexual wrong`
        THEN `s 56 does not apply: the injury came from an unlawful intentional act done to cause injury, or unlawful sexual assault or misconduct (s 6(4))`
        IF `an urgent proceeding not stayed`
        THEN `s 56 does not apply: my urgent proceeding was not stayed (s 43(5)(b))`
        IF `the award` GREATER THAN `the upper offer limit`
        THEN `s 56 does not apply: the award is more than the upper offer limit (s 56(1))`
        IF `the award` AT MOST `the lower offer limit`
        THEN IF `the award` AT LEAST `my final offer`
             THEN `costs to me on an indemnity basis from the day the proceeding started, and none before it (s 56(2)(b))`
             ELSE IF `the award` AT MOST `the respondent's final offer`
                  THEN `costs to the respondent on a standard basis from the day the proceeding started, and none before it (s 56(2)(c))`
                  ELSE `no costs are awarded either way (s 56(2)(a))`
        IF `the award` AT LEAST `my final offer`
        THEN `costs to me on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before the proceeding started, and on an indemnity basis from that day (s 56(3)(b))`
        IF `the award` AT MOST `the respondent's final offer`
        THEN `costs to me on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before the proceeding started, and to the respondent on a standard basis from that day (s 56(3)(c))`
        OTHERWISE `costs to me on a standard basis, up to the declared costs limit (s 56(3)(a))`

@export Who gets the legal costs if the court awards me damages no more than the upper offer limit (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) ss 6(4), 43(5), 56)? It depends on how the award compares with your mandatory final offer and the respondent's, and whether it is at or below the lower offer limit or between the lower and upper offer limits. The limits are fixed each financial year by the Minister's notice under s 75A; enter the ones that apply.
GIVEN `award` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages the court awarded you, in dollars
      `lower offer limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The lower offer limit fixed by the Minister's notice under s 75A for the relevant financial year, in dollars
      `upper offer limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The upper offer limit fixed by the Minister's notice under s 75A for the relevant financial year, in dollars
      `my final offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your mandatory final offer, in dollars
      `respondent's final offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the respondent's (or the respondents' joint) mandatory final offer, in dollars; 0 if it denied liability and offered $nil
      `intentional or sexual wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was caused by an unlawful intentional act (or omission) done with intent to cause personal injury, or by unlawful sexual assault or other unlawful sexual misconduct
      `urgent and not stayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding was started urgently with the court's leave and not stayed because of a terminal condition (s 43(4))
GIVETH A `Costs under s 56`
`Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` MEANS
    `s 56 -- costs` `award` `lower offer limit` `upper offer limit` `my final offer` `respondent's final offer` `intentional or sexual wrong` `urgent and not stayed`

-- s 48(1)(b): if the claimant does not comply with part 1, division 1, the court "may only award interest in the
-- claimant's favour for a period for which the claimant was in default if the court is satisfied there is a reasonable
-- excuse for the default" ("only if": JUST FALSE kind otherwise). s 48(1)(a): the respondent may also get its costs
-- caused by the default.
DECLARE `Interest for my default` IS ONE OF
    `not affected: I complied with the notice requirements (part 1, division 1)`
    `possible: the court may award me interest for the period I was in default, as it is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse (s 48(1)(b)); it may also award the respondent its costs caused by my default (s 48(1)(a))`
    `no: the court may not award me interest for the period I was in default without a reasonable excuse (s 48(1)(b)); it may also award the respondent its costs caused by my default (s 48(1)(a))`

GIVEN `I complied with division 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Interest for my default`
`s 48(1) -- interest for my default` `I complied with division 1` `the court is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I complied with division 1`
        THEN `not affected: I complied with the notice requirements (part 1, division 1)`
        IF `the court is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse`
        THEN `possible: the court may award me interest for the period I was in default, as it is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse (s 48(1)(b)); it may also award the respondent its costs caused by my default (s 48(1)(a))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the court may not award me interest for the period I was in default without a reasonable excuse (s 48(1)(b)); it may also award the respondent its costs caused by my default (s 48(1)(a))`

@export Can I get interest on my damages for the time I was in default of the notice of claim steps (Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) s 48(1))? Only if the court is satisfied you had a reasonable excuse for the default. The court may also award the respondent the costs your default caused it.
GIVEN `complied with notice steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you complied with the requirements of chapter 2, part 1, division 1 (notice of claim, and its time limits and responses)
      `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied you had a reasonable excuse for the default (for the court; answer as you understand it)
GIVETH A `Interest for my default`
`Can I get interest for the time I was in default` MEANS
    `s 48(1) -- interest for my default` `complied with notice steps` `reasonable excuse`
